From 1b8cece536ec1ee3ee9ac671dfacbc410024f073 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "xiu.yang" <xiu.yang@sophgo.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:18:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sensor): add gc4683 1920x1440 60fps linear and 30fps WDR
 modes

[description ]:
- Add SNS_TYPE GCORE_GC4683_MIPI_3M_60FPS_10BIT and
  GCORE_GC4683_MIPI_3M_30FPS_10BIT_WDR2TO1 to sensor_cfg with type names,
  getSnsObj/getPicSize(1920x1440)/getDevAttr(BAYER_GR, disEnableSbm) entries.
- Add GC4683_MODE_1920X1440P60 and GC4683_MODE_1920X1440P30_WDR with the
  vendor register sequences release_liner_v4.0.0_01 (1920x1440 60fps raw10
  linear) and release_raw10_hdr_v4.0.0_04 (1920x1440 30fps raw10 HDR),
  VTS 1600 / HTS 550 for both modes.
- Add the 1920x1440 AEC register tables (16-step linear, 14-step WDR LEF/SEF)
  and gain tables from the vendor AEC files; select gain/register tables per
  image mode instead of the fixed 2560x1440 tables, and take u32MaxAgain from
  the mode table.
- Reserve GC4683_1920X1440P30_WDR_SEXP_GUARD (80 lines) on the 3M WDR short
  exposure limit (u16SexpMaxReg, stExp[0].u16Max, cmos_fps_set u32Sexp_MAX)
  so the SEF readout ends at least 88 lines before the next SOF.
- cmos_set_image_mode matches 1920x1440 before the 2560x1440 range check,
  rejects fps outside the mode table, and refreshes u32FLStd/au32FL on mode
  switch; cmos_set_wdr_mode maps 1920x1440 linear <-> WDR.
- Behavior impact: BF01 (cv1815ja_bf01_spinand) can run GC4683 at
  1920x1440 60fps linear or 1920x1440 30fps WDR2TO1 selected by SNS_TYPE;
  existing 2560x1440/1080p/720p modes are unchanged.

[root   cause]:
- The driver only provided 2560x1440, 1920x1080 and 1280x720 sequences, so a
  1920x1440 request fell into the 2560x1440 mode via GC4683_RES_IS_1440P and
  the sensor streamed the wrong window; its AEC/gain tables also did not
  match the vendor 1920x1440 release.
- In 1920x1440 line-interleaved WDR the SEF readout trails the LEF by T1
  lines; with Sexp_MAX = VTS - 1440 - 8 the SEF ends only 8 lines (~166 us
  at 30fps) before the next SOF once AE reaches the limit. cv181x VI in HDR
  mode requires equal FE ch0/ch1 frame counts before BE/Post; the late SEF
  drops one ch1 frame, the counters never realign and
  _vi_event_handler_thread times out permanently (stall after ~18 frames).

[JIRA      ID]:CV180X181X-4655
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- Only the two new GC4683 modes and the shared table-selection helper are
  affected; other GC4683 modes keep their original tables and limits.
- Verified on BF01 hardware: 1920x1440 30fps WDR (VIDevFPS=VIFPS=30, FE
  ch0/ch1/BE/Post in sync to 2354 frames) and 1920x1440 60fps linear
  (VIFPS=60, 4718 frames), 0 vi_event_handler timeout, 0 frame-height
  errors, 0 CSI errors, boot burst capture 3/3. Register sequences and AEC
  tables verified against the vendor files item by item.
- No new issues observed.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :yoc.bin (BF01 fastboot small-core image); no *.ko/*.so

